   "id": "4bab353d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Data Cleaning / Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1ea4736",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "There were a couple attributes that needed cleaning, and we used these strategies for the following attribtues:\n",
    "- Pressure - 0.0 pressure is not a legitimate value, and we replaced those invalid values with the mean pressure of the dataset.\n",
    "- Missing values - any instance with a missing value is removed from the dataset.\n",
    "- Date - needs to be dropped, not a useful thing.\n",
    "- Precip-type - Since this has a ton of other values, it should be dropped.\n",
    "- All attributes - all remaining attributes besides the classification are continuous. They should be normalized."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b3644311",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "weather_data = MyPyTable().load_from_file(\"input-data/weatherHistory.csv\")\n",
    "weather_data.remove_rows_with_missing_values()\n",
    "weather_data.save_to_file(\"output-data/weatherHistory_cleaned.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "weather_data.replace_column(\"Formatted Date\", myutils.convert_date_to_numeric(weather_data.get_column(\"Formatted Date\")))\n",
    "# replace pressure zero values with mean\n",
    "\n",
    "weather_data.replace_column('Pressure (millibars)', myutils.convert_zeros_to_mean(weather_data.get_column('Pressure (millibars)')))\n",
    "weather_data.normalize_values([\"Formatted Date\", \"Temperature (C)\",\"Apparent Temperature (C)\",\n",
    "                               \"Humidity\", \"Wind Speed (km/h)\", \"Wind Bearing (degrees)\", \"Visibility (km)\", \"Pressure (millibars)\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "weather_data.save_to_file(\"output-data/weatherHistory_normalized_and_cleaned.csv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c87ffc60",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Loading data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9624fde1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "weather_data = MyPyTable().load_from_file(\"output-data/weatherHistory_normalized_and_cleaned.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "all_ys = [val[0] for val in weather_data.select_columns([\"Summary\"]).data]\n",
    "weather_x_data = weather_data.select_columns([\"Formatted Date\", \"Temperature (C)\", \"Apparent Temperature (C)\",\n",
    "                                      \"Humidity\", \"Wind Speed (km/h)\", \"Wind Bearing (degrees)\", \"Visibility (km)\", \"Pressure (millibars)\"])\n",
    "all_xs = weather_x_data.data\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c46bd9ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Should we use the boxplots to determine our discretizer? we could just discretize by mean (high low) or also use first and third quadrants. will probably need to explain our decisions in the presentation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2b64815c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# box plots for continuous data\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "weather_cts_data = weather_data.select_columns([\"Temperature (C)\", \"Apparent Temperature (C)\",\n",
    "                                      \"Humidity\", \"Wind Speed (km/h)\", \"Wind Bearing (degrees)\", \"Visibility (km)\", \"Pressure (millibars)\"]).data\n",
    "weather_cts_data_transposed = [list(row) for row in zip(*weather_cts_data)]\n",
    "\n",
    "for idx, data in enumerate(weather_cts_data_transposed):\n",
    "    # first, normalize it\n",
    "    new_data = myutils.norm_list(data)\n",
    "    ax.boxplot(new_data, positions = [idx], patch_artist=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(range(len(weather_cts_data_transposed)))\n",
    "ax.set_xticklabels([\"Temperature (C)\", \n",
    "                    \"Apparent Temperature (C)\",\n",
    "                    \"Humidity\", \n",
    "                    \"Wind Speed (km/h)\", \n",
    "                    \"Wind Bearing (degrees)\", \n",
    "                    \"Visibility (km)\", \n",
    "                    \"Pressure (millibars)\"])\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation = 45)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Distributions of Normalized Continuous Data\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Normed Values')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Box Plots of All Continuous Attributes')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "29c8c9d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Discretize each continuous row.\n",
    "Use mean or median based on whether outliers exist, since outliers have a pronounced effect on the mean and don't really affect the median."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "df03e34c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "num_features = 7\n",
    "weather_disc_data = []  # holds only discretized X columns\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(num_features):   # e.g. 7\n",
    "    new_col = [float(x) for x in weather_cts_data_transposed[i]]\n",
    "    crit_bool = (i == 4 or i == 5)\n",
    "    discretized_col = myutils.high_low_discretizer(new_col, crit_bool)\n",
    "    weather_disc_data.append(discretized_col)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add y separately\n",
    "ys = all_ys\n",
    "\n",
    "# Now transpose ONLY the X columns properly\n",
    "disc_prepped_weather = list(zip(*weather_disc_data))\n",
    "\n",
    "# X and y\n",
    "discretized_xs = [list(disc_prepped_weather[i]) for i in range(len(disc_prepped_weather))]"
   ]
  },
